desc: Channel Surfing Analog Channel Strip (AnalogChannel port) by chmaha
tags: processing channel strip console eq compressor expander saturation tape tube clipper analog
author: chmaha
version: 1.0
changelog:
  Initial release.
about:
  A complete analog-style channel strip in one window, in signal-flow order: Saturation In (Clean, Pure, Tape or
  Tube drive), Filters (high-pass 12 or 24 dB/oct, low-pass 12 dB/oct at Q 0.5 or 24 dB/oct, Normal or Bump
  resonance, before the dynamics or after the output stage), Clean Comp (a
  transparent peak compressor with a threshold and a Fast switch), Low Dynamic (below a threshold, either a
  downward expander or an upward lifter that brings up quiet detail), a four-band EQ (Baxandall-style bass and
  treble shelves, each with a Mid Cut control that moves its band edge away from the mids and scoops them, plus two
  bells whose Q follows the gain; even with every EQ knob at 0 the Baxandall shelves leave a gentle lift of about
  +0.9 dB around 2 kHz and a little near 20 kHz, part of the original's colour), Style Comp (Warm optical or
  Punch, with Comp In drive, makeup and mix, before or after the EQ), Console (Clean, Pure, Oxford, Essex or USA
  colour with drive), Out Stage (Clean, Pure, Tape, Tube, Hard Clip or Soft Clip) and the output level. Every
  section can be switched off on its own and fades in and out without clicks.
  Channel Variation gives the left and right channels the small differences of two real console channels (48
  channels in 24 pairs; Stereo uses both channels of a pair, Mono gives both sides the same channel).
  Input and output peak meters and gain-reduction lights for the two compressors and the output stage.
  Changes from the original: the filter slopes are labelled with their real values (the original says 18 dB/oct
  for the 24 dB/oct high-pass and 6/12 dB/oct for the 12/24 dB/oct low-pass), and Tape keeps its head bump after
  Saturation In or Out Stage has been switched off and on again (in the original it is lost until a reload; the
  hidden Tape Head Bump Fix slider set to Off restores that behaviour).
  Ported from AnalogChannel by Filippo Terenzi (KuramaSound)
  https://github.com/FilTer87/VST-AnalogChannel (GPL-3.0-or-later)
  Algorithms: Airwindows PurestDrive, ToTape8, Tube2, Baxandall2, Channel8, PurestConsole3, FinalClip and
  ClipSoftly by Chris Johnson (MIT); CL1B by JClones (MIT); Digital Versatile Compressor by Michael Gruhn (LOSER, GPL)
  JSFX version released under GPL-3.0-or-later
  Claude generated some of this code
